8. Data Architecture

8.1 Data Strategy

Use PostgreSQL for transactional data and JSONB only where a controlled property structure varies by design type. Store binary assets in object storage and keep metadata, ownership, checksums, and access state in PostgreSQL.

Use UUID primary keys. All mutable business tables should include:

created_at

updated_at

created_by where applicable

status

Optional optimistic-lock version

Use soft deletion for user-generated or commercially relevant records that may require recovery or audit.

