9.4 Versioning Rules

Published Ready Design versions are immutable.

New creator changes produce a new version.

Existing user sessions remain linked to the version on which they started.

Handoffs and exports record the exact version.

A design may be unpublished without deleting historical licences, sessions, or exports.

10. Taste Engine

10.1 MVP Input

The MVP uses curated image selections. Every test image has reviewed weighted style tags.

User actions may include:

Select.

Reject.

Skip.

Strong preference, if included in the interface.

10.2 Profile Calculation

For tag t, the initial profile weight can be calculated as:

raw_weight(t) = Σ selection_value(i) × item_tag_weight(i, t)

profile_weight(t) = normalize(raw_weight(t))

Where:

A selected image contributes a positive value.

A rejected image may contribute a controlled negative value.

Skipped images contribute zero.

Normalization converts the result to a stable comparison range.

The exact weights must be configurable and versioned rather than hard-coded.

10.3 Service Direction Calculation

A service direction stores a delta from the Main Taste Profile:

effective_service_taste = main_taste + service_direction_delta

This avoids duplicating the entire Taste Profile and makes inheritance explicit.

10.4 Future AI Enhancement

Later versions may use image embeddings to:

Classify uploaded references.

Discover similarity beyond predefined tags.

Recommend complementary directions.

Improve tag confidence.

The tag model remains useful for user-facing explanations even when embeddings are added.

11. Creative DNA

Creative DNA is a structured representation of a creative's work and capability.

11.1 Inputs

Approved portfolio item tags.

Services demonstrated by each item.

Sector experience.

Creative-declared services confirmed during curation.

Multidisciplinary or studio capabilities.

Optional operational data such as availability and project scale when collected later.

11.2 Aggregation

The MVP calculates a weighted Creative DNA vector from approved portfolio items. Curator-reviewed tags should have higher trust than unreviewed self-declared tags.

creative_tag_weight(t) = weighted_average(approved portfolio item weights for t)

Store the aggregation version and source portfolio set so the result can be recalculated and audited.

