16. Authentication and Anonymous Sessions

16.1 Progressive Authentication

Users can browse and begin temporary journeys without login. Authentication is required when an action establishes ownership or persistent collaboration, including:

Saving a design permanently.

Exporting or purchasing when required by licence.

Saving project needs and results across devices.

Selecting a creative.

Starting or entering a workspace.

Publishing creative content.

16.2 Anonymous Session Model

Create a server-side anonymous_sessions record linked to a secure opaque browser token. Temporary projects, taste sessions, and design sessions may reference it.

On signup or login:

Verify the anonymous token.

Verify that resources are still claimable.

Transfer ownership inside one transaction.

Rotate the anonymous token.

Record an audit event.

Prevent one anonymous session from claiming resources already owned by another user.

16.3 Token Strategy

Short-lived access token.

Rotating refresh token stored using secure browser protections.

Passwords hashed with a modern adaptive algorithm.

Role and resource ownership verified on every protected request.

Rate limits on login, signup, password reset, AI actions, and export creation.

